WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.629
Hank: Good morning John, and congratulations
on the release of The Fault in Our Stars trailer,

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:07.120
it was fantastic! But I have to say, that
I'm a little bit upset.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.150
You might not even know this, but the release
of that trailer happened roughly at the same

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:16.240
time as the release of a short film that I
did with Michael Aranda. And I feel, like

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.420
it's kind of been overshadowed and nobody's
seen it because of all the TFiOS mania.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.869
SO, I've decided that I'm gonna show it to
you all right now. Without further ado, ladies

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:30.869
and gentlemen, this is Hank and the Tree.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Yeah. Uh-huh. Michael and I did that as part
of the World Builders campaign. World Builders

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.030
is kind of like the Project for Awesome, except
that it's run by authors instead of YouTubers.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.840
For every $10 dollars you donate, you are
entered in a chance to win one of hundreds

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.310
of signed books, by dozens of authors, and
when they reach certain milestones, like in

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:21.910
my case 350,000 dollars, people do weird things.
So check it out, there's a link in the description.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:26.150
Now, as wonderful as Hank and the Tree is,
TFiOS trailer is amazing and I've watched

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:31.160
it like 50 times. So here are some of the
things that I have noticed. In-depth review

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.630
of The Fault in Our Stars trailer.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:37.190
Hazel's mum drives a 2012 Honda Accord - a
sensible choice. Monica drives a green Mitsubishi

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:41.020
Eclipse, which is not what Monica drives in
the book. In the book she drives green Ford

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:44.340
Thinderburp- Thunderburp?! She drives a Thunderburp!

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:48.330
Hazel apparently likes Pink Floyd: this shirt
is really old, like, Laser Show Pink Floyd

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.110
shirt, that you can't get anymore, but I found
one on eBay and I bought it!

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:54.510
She also likes Imagine Dragons, that poster
is from a show that they did in Denver. I

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.830
don't know how she got there...
AND, Hectic Glow Poster!

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:01.880
Her wardrobe is as expected; Chuck Taylors;
purple bra; Ceci n'est pas une pipe shirt.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.900
And of course, Augustus is wearing his signature
leather pterodactyl jacket. Not, it's not

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:09.210
made of pterodactyl leather, though that would
be amazing. People at the warehouse just noticed

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.550
that if you look at it a certain way it looks
like a pterodactyl.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:15.590
Important TFIOS landmarks include the Anne
Franke house, the bridge where John once stared

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:19.290
at us, the Literal Heart of Jesus, and the
vaguely paedophilic swing, seeking the butts

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.370
of children.
The "HG" on the ceiling probably stands for

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.960
"Hazel Grace", but maybe it stands for "Hank
Green", you don't know! And what's this on

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.890
the nightstand, a piece of paper, what is
that, you think it could be maybe a Venn diagram?

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:33.690
John, thank you for helping bring something
so cool into the world I am extremely excited

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:38.440
for you, and for me. I want to go see it and
it's still five months away?!

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.600
I know this has got to be a really freaky
time for you, like, I'm sure you are super

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:47.800
anxious, but it is going to be fantastic.
Congratulations, and I'll see you on Tuesday

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.700
(cut to black)
(Hanklerfish plush swims into frame)

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.870
Blub blub blub blub blub blub blub!
Oh my gosh it's a Hanklerfish! They're real!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:57.160
Available for pre-order at dftba.com and if
you want to get one of these posters you can't

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:00.120
cos' they were only available during the Project
for Awesome, I'm sorry!

